{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1258504-escape-from-prison-the-supernatural-way","id":1258504,"title":"Escape from Prison the supernatural way...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-01T22:58:05-07:00","id":1258504,"title":"Escape from Prison the supernatural way...","content":"Okay this clip reminds. Enid the low key supernatural way of escaping from Prison. As in you appear super human but not like fireball telekinesis superhuman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/6UVSE1JYhWQ\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/6UVSE1JYhWQ\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/6UVSE1JYhWQ\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/6UVSE1JYhWQ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So it\u2019s giving me ideas of the type of supernaturals like Werewolves who would go to prison, maybe death row, but not break out because they are fighting bands while in prison. Maybe with a fetish to appear as them in solitary confinement while they hunt, or maybe even a Bane is bound under the prison and they need to keep tabs up close. And they only escape last minute. Like I can see a high rank werewolf agreeing to do time or go on death row, the pack sneaking in to rescue him only to have him point out he needs to stay to guard the place, then a big omen happens and they escape using super durability, just taking a hanging/electrocution/lethal injection/firing squad and busting out last minute. Makes me think maybe some prisons kind of half know there is more out their the. Officially on paper.<br /> <br /> Other ideas are Mages using prison as a somewhat safe place to meditate/gonon seeking for a decade, or Vampires going their for th easy access to to food. Or hell a prison freehold that has changelings tending it from the inside.<br /> <br /> I remember the talk about Lasombra having their own submarine, so what about a secret black ops Prison half run by the technocracy to hide low key supernaturals like ghouls, werewolves and vampires till the actual technocrats step in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just the video inspired me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T06:42:23-07:00","id":1258530,"title":"","content":"Vampires probably want to feed where there's less surveillance. Modern prisions have very little privacy and lots of cameras.The only way I can see that working it's if the leeches in question own the prison, and even then only in a country with little regulations. Such a place would be very interesting indeed.<br /> <br /> There's nothing particularly safe about prison for mages (It's not like you can't be targeted there, think how in Death Note Kira kills criminals in their cells. Prisons offer little protection from competent magick users), but some mages may like the idea of going to prison for Paradigm related reasons (a Tytalus could see some prisons as a survival challenge) and some may just end in jail as consequence of their shenanigans and decide that breaking out would be more trouble than it's worth (and then they proceed to meditate they Arete up)<br /> <br /> I imagine werewolves with the correct technological Gifts and spiritual allies to tamper with the surveillance system will have little problem moving trough a prison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T07:09:40-07:00","id":1258533,"title":"","content":"Prison would be bad for most supernaturals. Just like most normals. It would be very difficult to go through the entire process of being put into prison without being forced into sunlight, making it a bad option for vampires even before you get into all of the surveillance. For a Tradition mage, prison would be exceedingly dangerous. Keep in mind that the Technocracy has a huge amount of control over the government. They could have corrupt guards help arrange your assassination even if they didn't have magick to help them. Plus, mages are usually physically human and vulnerable to attacks from humans, even mundane prisoners with no link to supernatural factions could pose a threat to many mages, or at least push them into using magick unnecessarily often. Plus, the Technocracy can probably monitor the security cameras in most places, including prison, which means that it is something that mages want to avoid.<br /> <br /> For a werewolf it would be bad too. The cameras mean that any use of supernatural power could be recorded. A prison would almost certain be associated with a very high Gauntlet and the Umbra near a prison would likely have all sorts of nasty banes. If Pentex learned that a Garou was in prison, they would be easy prey, especially with help of corrupt prison guards which are probably more common in WoD than real life.<br /> <br /> In the case of a mage or werewolf, prison would be more survivable with magic (Gifts or Sphere magick) that could manipulate technology. Even so, it would be like living in dangerous enemy occupied territory.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm saying that a prison game couldn't work, but I think that a supernatural would need some other reason to go to prison than it being a safe place to hide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-02T08:35:58-07:00","id":1258543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be very difficult to go through the entire process of being put into prison without being forced into sunlight, making it a bad option for vampires even before you get into all of the surveillance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yeah. There's that. Even if the prison it's regented by vampires a prisoner would need to get there first, and there's no way all the process is going to happen at night. I still think it may be an interesting setting, but getting <i>into </i>jail (legaly) it's more problem than it's worth<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a Tradition mage, prison would be exceedingly dangerous. Keep in mind that the Technocracy has a huge amount of control over the government. They could have corrupt guards help arrange your assassination even if they didn't have magick to help them. </div> </div> </div>That depends. Technocracy may or may not know that prisoner number X is a mage. If they were already on your trail, getting into prison it's more or less like serving yourself on a platter. But if they weren't, escaping in a disturbing or uncanny way may well set them on your trail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, the Technocracy can probably monitor the security cameras in most places, including prison, which means that it is something that mages want to avoid. </div> </div> </div>They can, but fortunately they don't have the resources to do it all the time everywhere. Otherwise being a Traditionalist just wouldn't be survivable.<br /> <br /> From the Technocratic perspective, dealing with mages isn't a job for mundane police nor mundane prisons. Since mages ain't going to get caught by the police...usually...it doesn't make a lot of sense to equip most jails with magick detecting technology (at least not more sense than equipping every night club or every store).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, mages are usually physically human and vulnerable to attacks from humans, even mundane prisoners with no link to supernatural factions could pose a threat to many mages, or at least push them into using magick unnecessarily often. </div> </div> </div>If tough humans can be at home in jail, it stands to reason that tough mages will have an easier time. Also not all prisons are equally dangerous (although those that are less so have a bigger chance of being under Technocratic soil). But it's true that being in jail isn't something all or even most mages would find safe.<br /> <br /> It may be worthy to mention that some mages do recruit in prison (there's a Flambeau character based on that idea in the OoH book, and there's a lot of factions with links to organized crime so it makes sense), but they certainly don't do that because prison it's &quot;safe&quot; in any way - they want to recruit dangerous people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-03T23:13:58-07:00","id":1258830,"title":"","content":"S03e08 of Dusk Till Dawn had a Vampire controlled prison with one of the Lords (original vampires) living in their for safety.<br /> We're talking South American Prison Mexico or below, very high corruption.<br /> <br /> But in WoD compared to the real world, there'd be more corruption, you could probably process the character (as their own request and influence, or another's) for it to be under the table and to do it all out of hours. Maybe to avoid media, avoid due process, whatever you want...<br /> <br /> The issue would be inside the Jails, where routine is normally going to be beat into Prisoners if they don't comply, why aren't you eating (or awake) at the right times. Regulations mean that you have to have your hour outside each side, you're not going to make us get in trouble with our bosses are you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T00:16:25-07:00","id":1258834,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m assuming yeah it\u2019s waaay more corrupt in WOD prisons. If they had it completely monitored then that would get in the way of the guards and Wardens making money. Every Prison movie and nosleeo prison story gives you ample reasons why cameras are turned off or ignored.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ever read or hear the story Fresh Fish?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-04T06:02:39-07:00","id":1258864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1258504-escape-from-prison-the-supernatural-way?p=1258830#post1258830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue would be inside the Jails, where routine is normally going to be beat into Prisoners if they don't comply, why aren't you eating (or awake) at the right times. Regulations mean that you have to have your hour outside each side, you're not going to make us get in trouble with our bosses are you?</div> </div> </div> </div>If the prision it's regented by vampires in a super corrupt country where due process can be made at night (I don't know if there's a country like that in real life) that wouldn't be a problem. It's easy enough to have some &quot;dangerous prisoners&quot; (vampires) permanently locked away in solitary confinement (they get out at night). No questions asked because the prisoners know what happens to those who ask too many questions <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}